<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.4.5: Practice</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00907</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.4.5: Practice</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4632a548-cfd5-48d4-9a04-fd9042fe5dad</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>Complete the following questions to practice the skills you have learned in this lesson.</para>
<!--Do not edit this div tag.  It must surround the interaction block-->
<div class="os-raise-ib-pset" data-button-text="Check" data-content-id="c2dcb316-5043-4cc7-ab07-b8b93415d527" data-fire-learning-opportunity-event="eventnameY" data-fire-success-event="eventnameX" data-retry-limit="2" data-schema-version="1.0">
  <!--Q1a-->
  <exercise data-content-id="3b03d196-7526-4071-b198-999c2e4d4c08" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result." data-solution-options="[&quot;To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Match each equation with a verbal description that represents the same function.</para>
      <para>\(f(x)=2x+4\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q1b-->
  <exercise data-content-id="234da651-94df-4ff5-af49-007f3ed47257" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2." data-solution-options="[&quot;To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(g(x)=2(x+4) \)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q1c-->
  <exercise data-content-id="bf984679-4679-4e9b-bd3b-85ae0fd95e57" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result." data-solution-options="[&quot;To get the output, add 4 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(h(x)=4x+2\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q1d-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5955ed6d-6f72-4398-bb5d-80cb2b9881a9" data-problem-type="dropdown" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4." data-solution-options="[&quot;To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 2.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 2, then add 4 to the result.&quot;, &quot;To get the output, multiply the input by 4, then add 2 to the result.&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>\(k(x)=4(x+2)\)</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  To get the output, add 2 to the input, then multiply the result by 4.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--2-->
  <exercise data-content-id="0d08ce71-3fc2-4a8f-a27e-c97d363f1731" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="1" data-solution="\(A(x)=25+10x\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(A(x)=25+10x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(B(x)=80-15x\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Functions \(A\) and \(B\) are defined by these equations.
          \(A(x)=25+10x\) \(B(x)=80-15x\) 
          Which function has a greater value when \(x\) is 2.5? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct!  Function A has a greater value because B(2.5)=42.5 and A(2.5)=50.</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.3. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q3-->
  <exercise data-content-id="998043ad-68ac-4dc6-b932-88437166f755" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(f(x)=2x-7\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(x)=2x-7\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=-3x+1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)= -5x+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=x-10\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which function is greater when \(x = 4\)? </para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(x)=2x -7\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>

  <!--Q4-->
  <exercise data-content-id="a6cbad77-b6a6-46d6-9940-8b2019b175a9" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(f(x)=2x-1\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(f(x)=x+1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=3x-3\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=2x-1\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(f(x)=x+2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Which function rule describes the table below: </para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              \(x\)
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              \(y\)
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              5
            </entry>
            <entry>
              7
            </entry>
            <entry>
              9
            </entry>
            <entry>
              11
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(f(x)=2x-1\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.3.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>


  <!--Q5-->
  <exercise data-content-id="5ea74f7e-7211-4aa4-ae4f-db4b69b5ad08" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(g(x)=2(x-4)\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(g(x)=2x-4\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g(x)=-4-2x\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g(x)=x -8\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(g(x)=2(x-4)\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Write a function \(g(x)\) for the following statement: to get the output, subtract 4 from the input, then multiply the result by 2.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(g(x)=2(x-4)\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.1. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q6-->
  <exercise data-content-id="ad08a7ed-c590-4281-852d-11570c6bce38" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="\(h(x)=5x+2\)" data-solution-options="[&quot;\\(h(x)=5(x+2)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h(x)=5x+2\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h(x)=x +2(5)\\)&quot;, &quot;\\(h(x)=x+2\\)&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Write a function \(h(x)\) for the following statement: to get the output, multiply the input by 5 and then add 2.</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(h(x)=5x+2\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.1.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q7-->
  <exercise data-content-id="c60f5cda-248c-45f1-b8d8-19fc43601821" data-problem-type="multiplechoice" data-retry-limit="3" data-solution="-7" data-solution-options="[&quot;7&quot;, &quot;1&quot;, &quot;-1&quot;, &quot;-7&quot;]">
    <problem>
      <para>Find the value of \(f(x)=−2x−3\) when \(x=2\).</para>
      </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! -7</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activity 4.4.2. </para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Q8-->
  <exercise data-content-id="e067d2ce-4e9a-4fe3-87c3-6fbb16068c95" data-problem-comparator="integer" data-problem-type="input" data-solution="8">
    <problem>
      <para>Examine the table below. Find \(g(2.5)\) using the rule for this table. </para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
        <thead/>
        <tbody>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              \(x\)
            </entry>
            <entry>
              1
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              3
            </entry>
            <entry>
              4
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
              \(g(x)\)
            </entry>
            <entry>
              2
            </entry>
            <entry>
              6
            </entry>
            <entry>
              10
            </entry>
            <entry>
              14
            </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      
    </problem>
    <solution>
      <para>Correct! \(g(x)=4x-2\), \(g(2.5)=8\)</para>
    </solution>
    <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response">
      <para>Try again. Revisit activities 4.4.4.</para>
    </div>
    </exercise>
  <!--Do not edit below this line-->
  <solution> </solution>
  <div class="os-raise-ib-pset-encourage-response"> </div>
</div></section>
</content>
